   ],
   "corrections": [],
   "notes": "Base is the Wilson-Carr-Mann 1996 ASW; the paper modifies it by supplying carbon (10 mM Na-succinate), N as 8.8 mM NH4Cl (equimolar substitution for the base ASW's 8.8 mM NaNO3, so nitrate is treated as replaced) and vitamins via 1 ml/L MAMS solution. P is the experimental variable (50 uM-1.73 mM) supplied as K2HPO4, phosphocholine (PC) or phosphorylethanolamine (PE), with a -P control. Grown aerobically (30 C, shaking); no reductant/anaerobic gas. Mo and B trace metals and all nine MAMS vitamins were absent from the prior component list and are the main recovered additions; hydrate forms for "
  },
